            <ArticleTitle>[Asymptomatic saphenous vein graft aneurysm: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the case of a 48-year-old man with a history of coronary bypass graft 15 years earlier. The follow-up by routine chest radiography showed a right paracardiac opacity, which MRI conformed to be an aneurysm of the saphenous vein graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
